      "program_name": "Launchpad workforce housing incentive, eastern Placer County (Transient Occupancy Tax through the TOT-TBID Dollars at Work program)",
      "administering_agency": "Placer County Executive Office, Economic Development and Housing (Timothy Cussen, Housing Specialist); Tahoe City office 775 North Lake Boulevard; funding recommended by the North Tahoe Community Alliance (NTCA) TOT-TBID Dollars at Work program",
      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "$200,000 per new multifamily or single-family unit created (category one), $125,000 per ADU and $50,000 per SRO unit, paid at completion once the workforce deed restriction is recorded. Funding: $1,000,000 inaugural NOFA (April 2025; $600,000 reserved for Steelhead Cottage Court in Kings Beach, 3 tiny-home units, and $125,000 for an accessible ADU) and $3,000,000 of new TOT approved February 3, 2026, for a 2026 NOFA pool of $3,275,000. The February 25 to March 18, 2026 round drew 12 applications (5 multifamily, 6 ADUs, 1 conversion; 55 units; $10,550,000 requested), with a lottery expected to reserve funds from mid-May 2026.",
      "per_unit_cap": "$200,000 per unit (new construction or conversion of non-residential or non-code-compliant space), $125,000 per ADU, $50,000 per SRO.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Units must be in unincorporated eastern Placer County within the Tahoe Truckee Unified School District boundary (outside avalanche hazard areas) and deed-restricted for occupancy by households with at least one full-time local worker (or equivalent) employed within the TTUSD area; no income limit, the restriction is workforce occupancy. The deed restriction follows the Workforce Housing Preservation Program form with an option to purchase.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "mixed-use"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "annual NOFA",
      "next_deadline": "2026 round closed March 18, 2026; awards by lottery from mid-May 2026. Staff will revise the guidelines with community input (survey August 2026) and return to the Board later in 2026; the next NOFA depends on NTCA recommending TOT for FY 2026-27 and later. Lease to Locals (homeowner incentives, $500,000 of TOT in FY 2025-26, administered by Placemate) continues alongside.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "unclear",
      "layering_notes": "placer.ca.gov (including DocumentCenter PDFs) sits behind Cloudflare and refused automated access on 2026-11-06; Board items were read from the County's GovDelivery agenda attachments (content.govdelivery.com/attachments/CAPLACER), the Legistar client 'placerca', state records and news coverage. Launchpad is a per-unit grant rather than a loan and is sized for small infill projects in Kings Beach, Tahoe City and the North Shore; a 10-unit workforce project could draw $2 million, which is meaningful against TRPA coverage and construction costs in the Basin. It pays only at completion, so it is bridge-financed. The workforce (not income) restriction means it does not fit LIHTC deals directly but can fund unrestricted middle-income units in a mixed-income project. TOT funds are County funds, so prevailing wage status is unclear under Labor Code 1720; confirm with the County. North Lake Tahoe TOT also funds the Workforce Housing Preservation Program and the Dollar Creek Crossing effort.",
      "source_url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/CAPLACER/2026/05/08/file_attachments/3645300/03A.pdf",
      "record_id": "1d1bc18543",
